== stability of the extrapolated A ==
A three-parameter fit through three points has ZERO residual, so no single
fit is an error bar.  What is informative is which basis is stable.

fit                                                 A    rel.err
log m/m + 1/m  (28,32,36)               -0.1737870386   0.002887
log m/m + 1/m  (24,28,32)               -0.1730071625   0.001614
log m/m + 1/m  (20,28,36)               -0.1727731077   0.002964
1/m + 1/m^2    (28,32,36)                -0.159442436    0.07989
log m/m only   (32,36)                  -0.1583382646    0.08626

The one tabulated basis omitting log m/m (1/m + 1/m^2) lands ~8.0% off and
the two-parameter log m/m fit ~8.6%, so the three-parameter fit with that
correction is doing real work and A then agrees with -log2/4 to a few parts
in 1000.  This is NOT independent corroboration of GLW's O(k log(k+1)):
the basis was chosen with that remainder already in mind.
